{"kind":"request","text":"Remove duplicated Work counts from the Work/Activity selector\n\nThe global `active` count is already shown where it has meaning and control: beside the Active filter checkbox in the Work view. The same number is repeated inside the top-level Work/Activity view selector, where it is clutter rather than navigation. The selector currently also carries the overlapping attention figure, duplicating the adjacent Work filters by the same pattern.\n\nKeep the main-view selector focused on choosing Work or Activity. Keep Work counts in the Work filter controls, where their scope and effect are visible.","body":{"branch":"request/work-toggle-count-clutter","conditions":"1. Remove the global active count from the Work button in the Work/Activity main-view selector.\n2. Remove other workload counts from that selector as the same duplication pattern; Work and Activity remain plain navigation labels with their icons and selected state.\n3. Keep active, attention, and closed counts in the Work filter controls, where each number is adjacent to the filter it describes and changes.\n4. Do not remove per-topic counts: those describe individual topics rather than duplicating the global navigation label.\n5. Preserve accessible names, selected-state semantics, responsive behavior, and keyboard/focus behavior for the main-view selector.\n6. Update component tests so the TopBar has no global Work counts and WorkDrawer remains the single visible owner of those filter counts. Run UI type-check/tests and `git diff --check`.\n7. Review names the Workroom UI surface layer; architecture and security contracts are unchanged. Complete the required architecture, security, and simplification conclusions before approval.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}